commit 914f61e75e0e72e578b8ecd705cbbc018a6cc2a9
Author: Uladzimir Klyshevich <vladimir.klyshevich@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 27 00:19:04 2026 +0300

    fix(app,fa_ui): review round 1 — host decorator composition + quota match (gh-2391)

    All five review threads on PR #2438:

    1. BLOCKING (wiring): decorateHostSession wrapped the auth-decorated
       stream, so the row-label decoration rewrote '401: …' to '[AIN] 401: …'
       before the host decorator saw it — _leadingStatus never matched and
       the one-shot bridge re-resolution never fired. The host decorator now
       sees the RAW provider stream (leading status + structured rate-limit
       intact); the row-label auth decoration wraps it from OUTSIDE, so a
       passed-through failure still names the row. Regression test composes
       the exact wiring shape.
    2. BLOCKING (quota): _validateStreamResponse re-renders a live 429
       through the structured rate-limit message — the profile's errorCode
       never appears in the rendered text, so the terminal notice could never
       match. _matchesHostQuota now reads the structured RateLimitInfo
       (errorType, rawBody) first, rendered text as the fallback for
       providers that keep the payload inline. Regression test feeds a
       structured 429.
    3. IMPORTANT: the auth-expired marker carried a stray space
       ('[[auth-expired: host]]'); now the canonical '[[auth-expired:host]]'
       the recovery handler compares.
    4. IMPORTANT (fa_ui): the host-quota insertion had split two existing
       doc comments; _authExpiredCard and authExpiredDisplayText have their
       docs back and _hostQuotaCard / hostQuotaLinkFrom carry only theirs.
    5. SUGGESTION: the host-restored snack is localized
       (hostSessionRestored, EN + RU) like every other chat_screen string.

    ai.teammate <agent.ai.native@gmail.com>

